config PARAVIRT_SCHED_HOST
	tristate "Paravirt scheduling host framework"
	depends on KVM
	help
	  Paravirtualized scheduling lets the host and a guest exchange
	  scheduling information through a shared memory region, so the
	  hypervisor can schedule vCPU threads more effectively -- for
	  example, boosting the priority of a vCPU thread while the guest
	  runs a latency-sensitive workload on it.

	  This option enables the host side framework, which attaches to KVM's
	  vCPU scheduling tracepoints and dispatches their events to a policy.
	  The policy itself is supplied as a kernel module or a BPF program.
	  Built as a module (pvsched), which depends on KVM.

	  If unsure, say N.

